==Ingredients==
===Pie crust===
* 8 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] (225 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) plain [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]
* 4 oz (110 g) [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]
* 2 oz (55 g) [[Cookbook:Lard|lard]]
* 1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] of [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]
* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] cold water
===Filling===
*4 McIntosh [[Cookbook:Apple|apples]]
*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]
*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]
*¼ cup [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]
*2 cups [[Cookbook:Water|water]]
*3½ tablespoons [[Cookbook:Cornstarch|cornstarch]]
*[[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]] juice (of ½ lemon)
*½ teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]

==Procedure==
===Pie crust===
#Rub flour, margarine, lard, and salt together until the mixture has the consistency of fine [[Cookbook:Bread Crumb|breadcrumbs]].
#Gently mix in 2 tablespoons water to make a soft but firm dough.
#Divide dough in half, then roll each half out on floured surface to the size you want your pie.
#Use one [[Cookbook:Pie Crust|crust]] to line your [[Cookbook:Pie and Tart Pans|pie pan]].

===Filling===
#Core, peel, and [[Cookbook:Slicing|slice]] the apples into ⅛–¼-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] (0.5–1 [[Cookbook:Centimetre (cm)|cm]]) segments.
#Add lemon juice to the apple segments.
#Transfer excess juices to the pie pan.
#Combine the sugar and water in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]]. Bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] over medium heat, stirring gently until the sugar dissolves and you get a [[Cookbook:Simple Syrup|simple syrup]]. Remove from the heat and let cool until just warm.
#In a separate bowl, mix the cinnamon, nutmeg, flour, and cornstarch.
#Combine the apples, spice mixture, and syrup in a bowl. [[Cookbook:Tossing|Toss]] well.
#Transfer the apple filling to the crust-lined pie pan.
#Cover the filling with the second pie crust and make three slits on top.
#Crimp the edges of the crust together, [[Cookbook:Pie Crust Edges|making a decorative border]] if desired.
#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] in the [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] at 350°[[Cookbook:Fahrenheit|F]] (175°C) for 60 minutes or until golden brown.
#Take out the pie and let cool.
#If desired, serve warm with [[Cookbook:Ice Cream|ice cream]], frozen custard, or frozen yogurt.

== Notes, tips, and variations ==

* You can also use 2 store-bought [[Cookbook:Pie Crust|pie crusts]] instead of making the dough from scratch.

